{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it","id":854757,"title":"Half-Vampires or something like it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-28T17:55:13-07:00","id":854757,"title":"Half-Vampires or something like it?","content":"So, I have been trying to track down a good write up of these for sometime for the nWOD. I know there was a write up in mirrors which had some decent points but didn't really do it for me. <br /> <br /> Then I started to to look through my Classic World of Darkness books and my various fantasy RPG's as well. The runner up was the version from Time of Thin Blood (would take some tweaking) to fit my idea. Then I dug out my Half-Damned book from KoE and the ones in there are my favorite. <br /> <br /> I would make them a minor template or maybe a maximum BP of 3?<br /> <br /> How else would you convert them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:56:58-07:00","id":854758,"title":"","content":"First edition had damphyr from Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead. They were the living children of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T17:58:57-07:00","id":854760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854758#post854758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First edition had damphyr from Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead. They were the living children of vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am unsure if I have that book. How do the feel? What are they like?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:13:02-07:00","id":854771,"title":"","content":"They're rocks for the waves that are vampires to crash upon.<br /> <br /> They have some special abilities depending on the clan they descend from and some all around abilities to counter vampire Disciplines. They have a Lure that entices members of their clan and sort of puts them through a horrible trial that's likely to end in the vampire falling into torpor unless they find a way out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:14:29-07:00","id":854773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854760#post854760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am unsure if I have that book. How do the feel? What are they like?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're very different. The dampyr labor under a double curse: their nature is a curse upon the dampyr and a curse upon the Kindred. Their blood is an unconscious honey trap for the Kindred, who find it irresistible but suffer greatly when they feed upon them. The dampyr herself gets resistance to mind-altering Kindred Disciplines, certain behavioral triggers for gaining and losing Willpower, a minor passive benefit (8-Again for three Skills) and a lesser active power based on the clan of her Kindred parent, the clan's corresponding bonus Attribute dot. Then they have access to some exclusive Merits. Probably not what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> There's a second edition book coming up called Half-Damned, which is going to cover dhampir. I don't know if Rose has said anything on what the plans are for dhampir in that book. Could be anything from a mechanical update of the same core idea to a complete reimagining.<br /> <br /> Half-Damned from KotE is one I'm largely unfamiliar with. What were the dhampyr in that book like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-28-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T18:45:54-07:00","id":854788,"title":"","content":"I really enjoyed their concept and how the fit into vampire society in Half-Damned.<br /> <br /> Basically they were the half dead and half alive children of vampires and mortals. This unusual physiology gave them benefits from both worlds. They converted firearms etc. to bashing, had extremely extended lifespans, had a blood pool and their own form of generation so to speak, got dots it disciplines, etc. They could also eat food, walk in the sunlight without issues, heal like a normal human could, etc.<br /> <br /> They had no fangs and did not have the kiss. They could eat raw meat (or drink blood from storage, etc) to regain blood points, heal, etc.<br /> <br /> Their nicknames were Jade Walkers.<br /> <br /> Being one usually made you an outcast in vampire society - but you weren't outright Hunted, etc. You kind of lived on the outskirts - like the elephant in the room or a dirty little secret. Your vampire parent was usually ahamed of you though a lot of the half damned who wanted to be a part of Vampire society usually served their vampire parent in someway to get their foot in the door.<br /> <br /> They had some specific merits - like Face which acted as status in vampire society. Then they had some they gave them fangs, etc.<br /> <br /> Just a pretty great interpretation of them in my opinion.<br /> <br /> I am hoping to give them a treatment in Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-28T19:29:26-07:00","id":854819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854773#post854773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a second edition book coming up called Half-Damned, which is going to cover dhampir. I don't know if Rose has said anything on what the plans are for dhampir in that book. Could be anything from a mechanical update of the same core idea to a complete reimagining.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Rose has stated anywhere yet how they're going to tackle dhampirs in Half-Damned. I know I put together some ideas, but I don't want to share them until we all know more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T01:24:33-07:00","id":854923,"title":"","content":"Hey, if there's multiple origins for them (as there is in Wicked Dead) you could easily say there's multiple types of dhampyr. Honey-trap curse type, Mirrors type, maybe one that's more or less a natural ghoul like in Masquerade... sky's the limit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:02:08-07:00","id":854935,"title":"","content":"My vision of dhampir is something a little more high-powered, closer to actual vampire level. They heal fast (on par with werewolves), they can learn Disciplines, they can raise Blood Potency potentially to 10 (though my initial idea is that they can only go up to 5 without diablerie), and they age more slowly. As a rather longtime fangirl of <i>Vampire Hunter D</i>, I wouldn't mind if they could &quot;vamp out&quot; and get a temporary power boost, but I did make them susceptible to frenzy and all it entails. I'd actually create special Merits for them (the short fiction piece I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/694975-second-edition-books?p=764463#post764463\">here</a> is an example) as well as Disciplines or Devotions (or both) unique to dhampirs. I had a few other things, but I don't want to get too into it yet.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs are the subject of my very first foray into the industry, so they hold a special place in my non-staked heart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:38:04-07:00","id":854948,"title":"","content":"I've actually been prodding around the idea of something similar. Mine basically work like a ghoul except a) they can drink blood like a vampire, b) they lose 1 vitae a day instead of per month and c) if they run out of vitae they take 1 lethal damage instead that can only be healed using it, which means if they go a week or so without feeding they just flat out die.<br /> <br /> I'm not too sure about how ageing would work, but given the consequences of not feeding it's probably best if they work like normal humans until a certain point when their powers awaken, and then just stop ageing from then on. Maybe have them age normally while they're in withdrawal or something. It's a work in progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:47:29-07:00","id":854951,"title":"","content":"I had it so that their lifespans increase as Blood Potency rises. They also naturally produce Vitae, albeit slowly, and it takes longer the more powerful they are. They can feed, but don't need to, although they gain some serious bonuses.<br /> <br /> I wanted to toy with the idea that although they are &quot;half-Damned,&quot; they're actually disturbingly idealized predators. Perfected, if you will. They have many of the strengths of humans <i>and </i>vampires, and no Beast. A ferocity in their hearts, sure, but that comes from being a perfect (supernatural) predator. The implications would actually be sort of disturbing to both dhampirs and vampires, that this impossible progeny (the name of the little pitch I wrote up) is <i>almost </i>like it was meant to be. They're the true power of the Blood when married to a vital, living form. It's why I wanted them to be more of a full template, because that's just how I like my half-vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T02:52:48-07:00","id":854952,"title":"","content":"They do sound pretty cool, although they seem to be lacking the kick in the balls that always seems to come with being a CofD supernatural somewhere down the line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:02:59-07:00","id":854955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854952#post854952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They do sound pretty cool, although they seem to be lacking the kick in the balls that always seems to come with being a CofD supernatural somewhere down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they do have their own issues. They're prone to bouts of rage like vampire frenzy, they suffer from variants of their parent clan's bane, and they suffer from thirst for blood. They can compete with true vampires (and the old story hook of dhampirs hunting vampires holds true here), or even contend with other creatures of the night. Doing so requires effort, risks danger, and both of those things tax a dhampir. They need Vitae. The more they fight, the more they hunt or strive with vampires, the more they must feed, or else struggle greatly to keep up. So for those who hunt bloodsucking monsters, it's a slippery slope to becoming one in turn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:12:30-07:00","id":854959,"title":"","content":"Still not seeing a big negative here, basically you made a vampire that doesn't have to spend blood to heal since they regen like a werewolf, can walk around in the sun and gets a little hangry if they push themselves.....<br /> <br /> Now if the only way they can fuel their healing or disciplines/stat boosts/what have you can only come from vampire vitae that's a pretty solid kicker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","user":"Dwight","date":".  Reasons! 03-29-2016, 06:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T03:31:02-07:00","id":854967,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if you want to try to reduce it down to misleadingly simple terms, sure. Anything could be made to sound not that negative. Werewolves get tremendous amounts of physical power in exchange for getting a little too worked up sometimes. All too easily done.<br /> <br /> Or, you could look at it the other way. Imagine being driven to hunt in a modern world that has left hunter-gatherer society behind. You have a wild ferocity in your heart, an inability to ignore what's in the shadows. An unholy hunger always gnaws at the back of your mind. You fight the urge to feed on people, <i>your </i>people, fellow humans. The rush and power of Vitae is just as alluring to a dhampir as it is a vampire. Because of their inherent volatility, these are passionate creatures; there are no timid dhampirs, no easy life for the half-Damned. I'd probably have them have some uneasy relationship with the day, certainly at least more comfortable at night. Theirs is a lifetime of struggle, wrestling with the power of the Blood and resisting the temptation to feed\u2014or giving in.<br /> <br /> They suffer from other weaknesses as I mentioned above. And they don't have all the vampire's strengths. Sure, they heal fast (not like a Gauru werewolf, though), but they don't shrug off damage like vampires do. They aren't immune to hunger, fatigue, and while they endure toxins and harsh elements better than mortals thanks to their gifts, they're not immune to those. They must sleep, they must breathe, and contend with pain like mortals do. Ultimately, these things may all &quot;balance out,&quot; and they're about on part with vampires, but that's not necessarily the goal. I wouldn't mind it, though. They are different, and in ways that make for good stories, which is fine by me. I wrote up everything in more detail in my pitch, but I don't want to share it all here yet.<br /> <br /> Edit: Also, imagine flying into a rage because some guy harasses you at a bar, and you beat him to within an inch of his life. As he lies there, his face battered, his blood covering your knuckles, you feel that pulsing heart, you taste the sweet scent of blood on the air, and it'd be so easy ... even if no one is watching. Maybe you leave before the cops arrive, and then wait for his friends to haul him out into the parking lot. How bad do you want that precious lifeblood? How hot does your anger yet burn? Can you control your savage urges?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":109,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","user":"Claire Redfield","date":". 03-29-2016, 06:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T07:54:52-07:00","id":855070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854967#post854967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Also, imagine flying into a rage because some guy harasses you at a bar, and you beat him to within an inch of his life. As he lies there, his face battered, his blood covering your knuckles, you feel that pulsing heart, you taste the sweet scent of blood on the air, and it'd be so easy ... even if no one is watching. Maybe you leave before the cops arrive, and then wait for his friends to haul him out into the parking lot. How bad do you want that precious lifeblood? How hot does your anger yet burn? Can you control your savage urges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, sounds like a werewolf except you're only tempted to drink their blood rather than eat their flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T08:24:13-07:00","id":855083,"title":"","content":"Ridiculous: No shapeshifting was involved.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there's no inherent urge to cannibalizing people in Werewolf save for sheer pragmatism. Vampire is about Gluttony. Werewolf is about Wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 03-29-2016, 11:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T11:17:58-07:00","id":855140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=854935#post854935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My vision of dhampir is something a little more high-powered, closer to actual vampire level. They heal fast (on par with werewolves), they can learn Disciplines, they can raise Blood Potency potentially to 10 (though my initial idea is that they can only go up to 5 without diablerie), and they age more slowly. As a rather longtime fangirl of <i>Vampire Hunter D</i>, I wouldn't mind if they could &quot;vamp out&quot; and get a temporary power boost, but I did make them susceptible to frenzy and all it entails. I'd actually create special Merits for them (the short fiction piece I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/694975-second-edition-books?p=764463#post764463\">here</a> is an example) as well as Disciplines or Devotions (or both) unique to dhampirs. I had a few other things, but I don't want to get too into it yet.<br /> <br /> Dhampirs are the subject of my very first foray into the industry, so they hold a special place in my non-staked heart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is along the lines of what I have been thinking for the most part and is what the original half damned book tried to do. <br /> <br /> I really love the concept of half dead and half alive as well.<br /> <br /> In a few days I hope to get something written up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:54:25-07:00","id":855226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855083#post855083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ridiculous: No shapeshifting was involved.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there's no inherent urge to cannibalizing people in Werewolf save for sheer pragmatism. Vampire is about Gluttony. Werewolf is about Wrath.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it wasn't obvious I was talking about themes, not exact power sets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T13:57:39-07:00","id":855228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855226#post855226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it wasn't obvious I was talking about themes, not exact power sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>See second paragraph that you quoted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:03:44-07:00","id":855229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855226#post855226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it wasn't obvious I was talking about themes, not exact power sets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically, it shares a lot with Vampire in general. The fighting an urge to feed and lash out, the distancing from humanity\u2014though in the case of dhampirs, it's a different struggle than for full vampires, who have left mortality completely behind. But we might as well be saying that Vampire is like Werewolf except you're only tempted to drink their blood, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:14:17-07:00","id":855233,"title":"","content":"One idea I like is making the Dhampirs natural vampire hunters. Maybe a template ability which allows them to intuit a Vampire's banes? Heck, maybe a special merit or set of merits that replicate or counter the Disciplines in a anti-vampiric fashion, with the Dhampir getting their parent's Proprietary Clam Discipline-linked power for free?<br /> <br /> Probably a stupid idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:35:48-07:00","id":855248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855083#post855083\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ridiculous: No shapeshifting was involved.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, there's no inherent urge to cannibalizing people in Werewolf save for sheer pragmatism. Vampire is about Gluttony. Werewolf is about Wrath.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say Vampire is about Addiction and Werewolf is about Loyalty. But YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:37:32-07:00","id":855250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855248#post855248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say Vampire is about Addiction and Werewolf is about Loyalty. But YMMV.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm drawing thematically from sins. Mage falls squarely into Pride.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:41:50-07:00","id":855255,"title":"","content":"Also, Loyalty over Wrath? Lol no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:41:57-07:00","id":855256,"title":"","content":"Sins are 1e and really Judeo-Christian. So definitely YMMV. But also, the 2e games don't fit to well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T14:48:17-07:00","id":855261,"title":"","content":"Forsaken may not have a <i>trait </i>called Rage, but it's still a pretty damn strong theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-29T16:20:41-07:00","id":855318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=855261#post855261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forsaken may not have a <i>trait </i>called Rage, but it's still a pretty damn strong theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Our opinions differ. No reason to be denigrating about it.<br /> <br /> Also apparently quoted the wrong post...(stupid smart phones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T09:47:10-07:00","id":857171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it#post854757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I have been trying to track down a good write up of these for sometime for the nWOD. I know there was a write up in mirrors which had some decent points but didn't really do it for me.<br /> <br /> Then I started to to look through my Classic World of Darkness books and my various fantasy RPG's as well. The runner up was the version from Time of Thin Blood (would take some tweaking) to fit my idea. Then I dug out my Half-Damned book from KoE and the ones in there are my favorite.<br /> <br /> I would make them a minor template or maybe a maximum BP of 3?<br /> <br /> How else would you convert them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've actually been working on homebrew dhampir rules. I'd be curious to get people's response:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YQ_lztn_gV4-AnFC19CCH5Ek4iaA9MzyV8U5hd8seGY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YQ_lztn_gV4-AnFC19CCH5Ek4iaA9MzyV8U5hd8seGY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YQ_lztn_gV4-AnFC19CCH5Ek4iaA9MzyV8U5hd8seGY/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1YQ_lztn_gV4-AnFC19CCH5Ek4iaA9MzyV8U5hd8seGY/edit?usp=sharing </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I based them thematically on Time of Thin Blood -- half-breeds who have access to vampiric power, but have to deal with the Beast (among other complications). Power level-wise I tried to situate them in between ghouls and younger vampires. Most of the rules are lifted verbatim from the ghoul character creation rules and I modified and added rules to address dhampir-specific traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11557-jojo11","name":"jojo11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T11:19:26-07:00","id":857205,"title":"","content":"I would treat them like ghouls with a fewer significant differences;<br /> \u200b1-They can take vitae directly from the source, no Vampire filter required.<br /> 2-They don't suffer ghoul negatives when they go without, such as rapid aging.<br /> 3-Without a Vampire patron they take their discipline from their sire's clan.<br /> 4-If they have no vitae in their system they run the risk of frenzy.<br /> 5-If they are not cremated or embraced they will rise after death as a Revenant.<br /> The goal would be to tempt them with blood drinking, while simultaneously making them a potential threat to both Kin and Kine.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-01T21:26:41-07:00","id":857471,"title":"","content":"There's also, if memory tricks me not, an anternate version of the half-vampire idea in the Woundgate setting from Mirrors, in case it hasn't been mentioned so far.<br /> Bringing it up for a possible alternate example for comparison, contrast, or mix-&amp;-matching.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-02T18:08:55-07:00","id":858051,"title":"","content":"So - here is what I am leaning towards....it's a rough outline...<br /> <br /> Use Chronicles of Darkness Character Creation with the following changes:<br /> <br /> 1. Concept: decide on concept and select three Aspirations for your character<br /> 2. Achors- Select a virtue and vice<br /> 3. Attributes 5/4/3<br /> 4. Skills 11/7/4<br /> 5. Choose 3 skill specialties <br /> 6. 10 dots of merits<br /> 7. Calculate advantages - use Integrity <br /> <br /> Add Dhampir template<br /> <br /> 1. Add both bonus dots from your parent clans favored attributes<br /> 2. BP starts 1 - can spend 5 merit points to increase it by 1. Max BP 5 without diablrie<br /> 3. They are susceptible to Frenzy with a more focus on hunger<br /> 4. 3 dots for disciplines. All physical disciplines are considered in clan. <br /> 5. Vitae regenerates 1 PT a week<br /> 6. Do not have fangs/kiss without spending a Vitae <br /> 7. All mundane damage considered bashing, can spend vitae to heal and all other normal vamperic uses<br /> 8 need a list of special merits like stake combat, poisoned vitae, resistant to bnlood bonds, etc. This is going to be the harder part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No live organism can continue for long to exist sanely under conditions of absolute reality; even larks and katydids are supposed, by some, to dream.&quot; - Shirley Jackson","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1227-shenron","name":"Shenron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T06:38:30-07:00","id":858308,"title":"","content":"Sorry to butt in, but the tidbit about werewolves made me wonder:<br /> <br /> What a bout a half-vampire, half-werewolf? Possibly through some weird occult shenanigans involved, like the Coil of \u017diva? I find the idea of a mortal with both vampiric and wolfen blood to be quite interesting. It'd be the most Frenzy-prone creature in the CofD, possibly, but figuring out all the quirky interactions between the advantages and disadvantages of both lineages would be a good thought exercise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:11:27-07:00","id":858324,"title":"","content":"Well, vampires with a wolfblooded tell are a thing. How certain ones work exactly is a matter of debate. As for the full hybrid. That was a thing in the Classic World of Darkness. It was called an Abomination, and is a bit of a controversial topic. There's a thread somewhere on here where a few of us batted around ideas on how to implement them in the CofD in such a way that they didn't feel out of place. My idea was to make them the products of an Idigam experiment. The Strix are another possible culprit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","user":"Elfive","date":". 04-03-2016, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T07:23:56-07:00","id":858330,"title":"","content":"Well, I was reading up on the Coil of \u017diva, and it has a part where, after using the 5-dot power (which turns you into an actual human), you have a half-hour where you experience the Embrace all over again. Half an hour is enough time for copulation, so if we say that the werewolf partner is in Dalu, perhaps the metaphysical resonances are such that they create a perfect hybrid.<br /> <br /> In fact, &quot;creating a perfect werewolf-vampire hybrid&quot; might well be a good hook for an Ordo Dracul antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/872434-shadow-knight-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10056-shadowknight1224","name":"ShadowKnight1224","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"975"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T10:41:02-07:00","id":873866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shenron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=858051#post858051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Add both bonus dots from your parent clans favored attributes<br /> 2. BP starts 1 - can spend 5 merit points to increase it by 1. Max BP 5 without diablrie<br /> 3. They are susceptible to Frenzy with a more focus on hunger<br /> 4. 3 dots for disciplines. All physical disciplines are considered in clan.<br /> 5. Vitae regenerates 1 PT a week<br /> 6. Do not have fangs/kiss without spending a Vitae<br /> 7. All mundane damage considered bashing, can spend vitae to heal and all other normal vamperic uses<br /> 8 need a list of special merits like stake combat, poisoned vitae, resistant to bnlood bonds, etc. This is going to be the harder part.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like a daywalking vampire but better in every way.<br /> Licks take bashing damage from most sources because they don't need/use their organs or bodily systems(respiratory, circulatory, etc) to survive.<br /> Also as purer expressions of the beast, which should probably be weakened in dhampirs, perhaps the clan unique disciplines should be inaccessable or restricted to 2 dots out of clan or 3 dots from sire's clan max?<br /> <br /> One complication that they do appear to have in your template is the inability to hide their feed by licking the wound, which could make for some interesting feeding scenes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T09:19:37-07:00","id":875720,"title":"","content":"Going with Claire's vision, I'd actually double down on the werewolf similarities and give the dhampir an Integrity equivalent that works a bit like 2e Harmony, where on one end you're almost human but limited in power, and on the other you are almost entirely a vampire, with all the power it entails but also many same banes. I believe this would work great for dhampir as vampire hunters, creating a perverse incentive for them to become more and more like the thing they hunt in order to keep up power-wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:03:21-07:00","id":876490,"title":"","content":"Ghouls fit a lot that people seem to think of for dhampir, and revenants are already the 'almost Vampires but not technically' so I don't know about Claire's dhampir here. For Half-damned I wouldn't mind seeing something like Wicked Dead but I'd like to see something different, too","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:39:06-07:00","id":876512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876490#post876490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls fit a lot that people seem to think of for dhampir, and revenants are already the 'almost Vampires but not technically' so I don't know about Claire's dhampir here. For Half-damned I wouldn't mind seeing something like Wicked Dead but I'd like to see something different, too</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are dependent on vampires - servitude and addiction is the price they pay for vampire powers. Revenants are &quot;vampires but worse&quot; - all the same (or worse) weaknesses, fewer advantages.<br /> <br /> What Claire proposes is something roughly on par with vampires, if not better than them. Something inspired by such characters as D, Alucard (the Castlevania one) or even Blade, a figure vampires would both envy and fear.<br /> <br /> I understand why people might not be down with this vision, but to say it's redundant with either ghouls or revenants is way off the mark.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:42:26-07:00","id":876517,"title":"","content":"I had a very simple dhampir Merit, which granted the ability to sense vampires (including Obfuscated ones), plus immunity to blood bonds and vitae addiction, but came with sickliness from the death under their skin (the no 10-again and 1's taking from successes weakness pattern, applied to physical rolls).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:46:20-07:00","id":876523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876512#post876512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouls are dependent on vampires - servitude and addiction is the price they pay for vampire powers. Revenants are &quot;vampires but worse&quot; - all the same (or worse) weaknesses, fewer advantages.<br /> <br /> What Claire proposes is something roughly on par with vampires, if not better than them. Something inspired by such characters as D, Alucard (the Castlevania one) or even Blade, a figure vampires would both envy and fear.<br /> <br /> I understand why people might not be down with this vision, but to say it's redundant with either ghouls or revenants is way off the mark.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well there are ghoul families which are 99.9% the same already.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, your idea about the harmony scale is interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-28-2016, 08:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T05:48:06-07:00","id":876526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876512#post876512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand why people might not be down with this vision, but to say it's redundant with either ghouls or revenants is way off the mark.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T06:50:06-07:00","id":876584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876523#post876523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well there are ghoul families which are 99.9% the same already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can I make a Blood Potency 5 vampire hunter who's able to go toe to toe with the city's elders using ghoul families? I honestly don't remember them that well, but somehow I doubt it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T02:15:26-07:00","id":877474,"title":"","content":"I think it'd be fun, either way, and the thing I'm most looking forward to playing is a dhampir. This book will totally knock it out of the park, I'm sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:47:42-07:00","id":877531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876584#post876584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I make a Blood Potency 5 vampire hunter who's able to go toe to toe with the city's elders using ghoul families? I honestly don't remember them that well, but somehow I doubt it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that would have to be edited is their inability to gain Blood Potency, and their inability to transubstantiate consumed blood into Vitae, then yes.<br /> <br /> I'm not seeing a a mechanical effect for ghoul families in the 2E book at this moment, just a reference on pg 296 - 297, but basically in the real difference was that they generated 1 vitae per month naturally.<br /> <br /> Ghouls really are half-vampires already, they just can't feed directly so a couple small changes and you have a ready-made Dhampir template!<br /> Check out pg 297 for the ghoul template.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 04-29-2016, 06:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T07:55:23-07:00","id":877693,"title":"","content":"A ghoul who generates one Vitae per month is pretty far off from the badass regenerating daywalker Claire proposed. Not that it's an objectively bad thing, mind you. Just not what I'm thinking about at the moment.<br /> <br /> I'm in the middle of writing up my own version of dhampir, heavily inspired by Claire's posts. If anyone's interested, I'll post a draft when it's remotely presentable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T13:09:43-07:00","id":878019,"title":"","content":"I look forward to seeing what you come up with, Morangias.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=876512#post876512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Claire proposes is something roughly on par with vampires, if not better than them. Something inspired by such characters as D, Alucard (the Castlevania one) or even Blade, a figure vampires would both envy and fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one thing I'd be a little careful of is making dhampirs <i>too </i>much better than vampires, if at all. I mean, I like the idea of hinting that this unnatural combination is somehow <i>right</i>, like a step on the path to becoming a more perfected supernatural predator. But I'd also make sure to emphasize that even if they are a vision of &quot;perfected&quot; vampirism, somewhere between mortal and immortal, a predator without equal and without flaw, there's a price to pay. Weaknesses. Bloodlusts that no human endures; not even the most bloodthirsty mortal killer understands an actual thirst for blood in the same way a dhampir does. All of those burning passions within her grow to an inferno when the Blood calls to her. She can never be truly &quot;perfect&quot; without the sweet nectar of life fueling her, transforming her into an exquisite engine of predation. What more the cost of tearing into a neighbor, a friend, a loved one, to drink deep of that most potent elixir, when you're not so far removed from them as your vampire kin? Then again, given your actions ... maybe you are.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T19:38:15-07:00","id":878358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Claire Redfield</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=878019#post878019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I'd be a little careful of is making dhampirs <i>too </i>much better than vampires, if at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to agree. As it is, ghouls already have access to the most notable abilities of vampires, in Disciplines, and none of their weaknesses. While it's easy to dismiss ghouls as mindlessly subservient slaves, that's really up to the regnant. They're capable of learning all the primary Disciplines, even performing some rituals, have limited immortality and through Physical Disciplines can have inhuman Attributes. Aside from the idea of 'privileged' ghouls who are held in better esteem than that of slave, there's rogue ones who are capable of bringing down vampires.<br /> <br /> It's very easy to have something that's better than a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T20:22:25-07:00","id":878386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=878358#post878358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree. As it is, ghouls already have access to the most notable abilities of vampires, in Disciplines, and none of their weaknesses. While it's easy to dismiss ghouls as mindlessly subservient slaves, that's really up to the regnant. They're capable of learning all the primary Disciplines, even performing some rituals, have limited immortality and through Physical Disciplines can have inhuman Attributes. Aside from the idea of 'privileged' ghouls who are held in better esteem than that of slave, there's rogue ones who are capable of bringing down vampires.<br /> <br /> It's very easy to have something that's better than a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily mind dhampirs being &quot;better&quot; than ghouls, though. If I did it the way I'd talked about earlier in the thread, they certainly would be. And I don't mind the idea of them seeming from an OOC perspective to have it better than vampires, possessing the strengths without being undead. But I wouldn't want to go the &quot;all of their strengths, none of their weaknesses&quot; route. They should blend the strengths and weaknesses of both, and probably add some unique traits to the mix. &quot;Like a vampire, but better in every way&quot; doesn't really capture what I'd want to do with it. So you just have to be careful with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-01T15:09:14-07:00","id":879715,"title":"","content":"I am WAITING (rather impatiently) For some snippets from Half Damned or thousand years of night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T04:22:52-07:00","id":880039,"title":"","content":"Very long time lurker on the boards, but this thread inspired me to try my hand at homebrew and this is it, id be curious as to peoples response to it.<br /> I made them very similar to true vampires and the was pretty much my purpose- to have them feel almost like a very odd bloodline and to keep them close to the real deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mhsl3iGrmNG6F1RW1t1b8rccwvZxXW53RNG2ON9-Z4c/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mhsl3iGrmNG6F1RW1t1b8rccwvZxXW53RNG2ON9-Z4c/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mhsl3iGrmNG6F1RW1t1b8rccwvZxXW53RNG2ON9-Z4c/edit?usp=docslist_api\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Mhsl3iGrmNG6F1RW1t1b8rccwvZxXW53RNG2ON9-Z4c/edit?usp=docslist_api </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11687-gwindilin","name":"gwindilin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:22:24-07:00","id":885065,"title":"","content":"oh Revenants, ideas what we'll get for them in the new book? more ways they can be &quot;Promoted&quot; to full vampires.<br /> <br /> special merits? ideas on playing one.<br /> <br /> oh curious issue, think Revenants are ever accepted by kindred to any degree, <br /> <br /> do you think being a former revenant, is that big a blight on a vampires history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T18:52:38-07:00","id":885076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowKnight1224</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=858330#post858330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I was reading up on the Coil of \u017diva, and it has a part where, after using the 5-dot power (which turns you into an actual human), you have a half-hour where you experience the Embrace all over again. Half an hour is enough time for copulation, so if we say that the werewolf partner is in Dalu, perhaps the metaphysical resonances are such that they create a perfect hybrid.<br /> <br /> In fact, &amp;quot;creating a perfect werewolf-vampire hybrid&amp;quot; might well be a good hook for an Ordo Dracul antagonist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't the blush of life honestly allow copulation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T19:26:23-07:00","id":885095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=885076#post885076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't the blush of life honestly allow copulation?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I read it, yes, it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T07:14:24-07:00","id":885353,"title":"","content":"why do all Fan write ups I've seen for Dhampires in 2nd edition dispense with the lure? I thought it was cool and evocative...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T11:48:27-07:00","id":885540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=885353#post885353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">why do all Fan write ups I've seen for Dhampires in 2nd edition dispense with the lure? I thought it was cool and evocative...</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they swallowed the hook! har har...<br /> On a more serious note though, what lore are you looking for? The 1E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T06:46:25-07:00","id":886174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=877693#post877693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghoul who generates one Vitae per month is pretty far off from the badass regenerating daywalker Claire proposed. Not that it's an objectively bad thing, mind you. Just not what I'm thinking about at the moment.<br /> <br /> I'm in the middle of writing up my own version of dhampir, heavily inspired by Claire's posts. If anyone's interested, I'll post a draft when it's remotely presentable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Somebody please explain the need or attraction of this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:33:20-07:00","id":886224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=886174#post886174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Somebody please explain the need or attraction of this idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some people really like Vampire Hunter D. Or Castlevania. Or even Blade.<br /> <br /> Some people may want to introduce a vampire hunter who's not just dangerous because he's savvy and sets up great ambushes, but one that will give the coterie a run for their money when they finally confront him.<br /> <br /> Some people may want to play a vampire in a mixed game, but don't want to hold the rest of the team back with their inability to operate in daytime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T17:34:20-07:00","id":886789,"title":"","content":"IIRC, the 1e dhampirs were rather clearly inspired by Vampire Hunter D. <br /> <br /> While I think there should be options for building a character that way (i.e., through merits), I don't see the need for every dhampir to be a highly skilled vampire slayer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T19:24:52-07:00","id":886872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/854757-half-vampires-or-something-like-it?p=886224#post886224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some people may want to play a vampire in a mixed game, but don't want to hold the rest of the team back with their inability to operate in daytime.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep your humanity up and wear your riding leathers out. It won't be much of an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link"